## Original Content
When Twitch announced that streamers could opt out, thousands of users questioned why their content was being used to train AI models in the first place.

## Summary
Twitch streamers' content is used by Amazon to train AI models, prompting thousands to question the practice after being given an opt-out option. Streamers can now choose to prevent their content from being used for this purpose. The move highlights concerns over data usage and privacy.

## Key Points
- Twitch (owned by Amazon) uses streamer content to train AI models
- Streamers have been given the option to opt out of content usage for AI training
- Thousands of users expressed surprise and concern over the initial lack of transparency


